\p{SUPERSEDED (2026-11-24T23Z): this fragment was the "Warm wall clock" section that \src{bench/track/benchmarks_cold.py} appends to its cold tables. \src{docs/BENCHMARKS.md} is now generated by \src{bench/track/benchmarks.py} from the rows of \src{bench/warm.sh} and no longer includes it; the rows below (wave-6 integration, machine \code{\verb~|78c74ca92785~}, the launcher line before 22Z, \code{\verb~|-X load=pipelined~} given by hand) are kept as the record of that distribution.}

\p{Owner note 12: the target is the wall clock of checking in steady state - the same process checks the same export again (\code{\verb~|rlvm -X passes=N~}, rlvm-main/README.md "Passes"; tool \src{bench/warm.sh}, bench/README.md "Warm wall clock"). Every pass is a complete run (load pipelined with checking, new store and engines; \code{\verb~|-X passes-mode=reload~}); warm = median of passes 2..N of one process (best in brackets); \code{\verb~|--threads 8~} on the 8 measurement cores inside a \src{bench/quiet.py} window, on the host (not in the arena container); heap 6 GB for the small corpora, the launcher's own 13 GB for the large ones. Baselines: the arena's run line with 8 (and 1) threads in the arena container on the same cores, second of two runs. Not the arena's configuration and not comparable with the cold tables above cell by cell (those are batch loads in the container). Two tables: the machine of the wave-6 integration, and the first warm table of 17:37Z (kept: it has the reference engine, the generic tier and the recheck rows).}

\subtree{
\title{The machine with its default switch set of wave 6 (windows of 20:04Z - 20:30Z)}

\p{Distribution \code{\verb~|work/int6/dist-b~} (machine \code{\verb~|78c74ca92785~}: in THIS distribution the machine is the default engine - it was from 19:41Z to 20:35Z and is not any more, see \src{rlvm-machine/SWITCHES.md}; the rows are what \code{\verb~|-X engine=machine~} gives today - with the switch set \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,bodies,pchk,match,joint,code,casetrees,lazycases,directrules,lazyeval,same~}, cap 1 MiB; rlvm-driver \code{\verb~|31fa08d9ce61~}, rlvm-load \code{\verb~|492a436c2c95~}, rlvm-ref \code{\verb~|ca1f9bd918bb~}; CE native image \code{\verb~|-O3~}; JVM launcher as shipped: HotSpot C2, SerialGC), no \code{\verb~|-X engine~} and no switch list. N = 5 on the native image (3 for navier-stokes-euler and cslib, 2 for mathlib; 3 for one worker), on the JVM launcher 10 for Init, 6 otherwise, 3 for mathlib. gruszka and nano-lean were measured in the SAME windows. Rows: \code{\verb~|work/perf-history/warm.tsv~}, label \code{\verb~|int6-final~}; scripts \code{\verb~|work/int6/wA.sh~}, \code{\verb~|wB.sh~}.}

