\p{What it says. (1) In steady state with 8 threads on the same cores the machine (native image) is at 1.23 times gruszka on Init (0.81 against 0.66 s), 1.42 on Std, 1.26 on cedar, 1.41 on the Cedar slice, 0.26 on reachability and 2.23 on mathlib (27.4 against 12.3 s; the JVM launcher: 21.2 s = 1.72 times); against nano-lean 0.78 / 0.87 / 0.77 / 0.94 / 0.81 / 1.48 (JVM launcher on mathlib: 1.15). (2) Against the first warm table below (\code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}, other pipeline jars): native image Init 1.07 -> 0.81 s, Std 1.88 -> 1.51, cedar 2.62 -> 2.08, reachability 2.66 -> 0.61, con-leche 2.18 -> 1.77, navier-stokes-euler 9.29 -> 8.35, cslib 9.06 -> 7.61, mathlib 35.3 -> 27.4; JVM launcher mathlib 25.6 -> 21.2. (3) The JVM launcher is not steady within these pass counts on Std and cedar (its walls still fall in the last passes: read its "best", and the 10-pass rows of the first table); once steady it is the faster platform on Init, reachability and mathlib, as before. (4) One worker (native image): Init 4.40 s, Std 8.68, reachability 1.44, Cedar slice 1.91; gruszka with one thread 3.07 and 4.51 on Init and Std, nano-lean 4.58 and 8.20.}
}

